// AUTO-GENERATED by scripts/50_export_dashboard_data.py (scripts/vintage_engine.py).
// Do not edit by hand.
//
// Vintage analysis: per (ticker, vintage_year, age_quarters) cumulative credit
// performance curves (dating engine restored 2026-09-25, with fixes).
//
// "Vintage" is assigned per loan by a dating waterfall (best evidence wins):
//   1. own_acq           — holder's own disclosed acquisition date (earliest
//                          ever printed); overridden when a peer holding the
//                          SAME tranche (lien match, maturity ±2y) disclosed
//                          >90d earlier, or on amendment-retag evidence.
//   2. xbdc_borrow       — tranche-matched date from a peer BDC's SOI.
//   3. ltail_enriched    — name-matched date from a long-tail fund's XBRL.
//   4. xbdc_borrow_loose — date from a DIFFERENT facility of the borrower.
//   5. dera_lower_bound  — earliest long-tail sighting of the borrower.
//   6. tenor_model       — maturity − calibrated tenor (stable-loan median).
//   7. first_obs_*       — first parsed observation (requires reliable
//                          prior-quarter coverage; maturity/discount clips).
// Sources 3-7 are ESTIMATES, graded LOW. 1-2 are graded by disclosure
// stability (HIGH ≤90d drift/spread, MED ≤12mo, else LOW). A date more than
// two quarters AFTER our first sighting of the loan is rejected (next source
// wins); an own date replaced that way by a same-tranche peer date or a
// reliably-covered first sighting counts as a correction (MED). These are
// acquisition / first-seen dates, not proven facility origination dates.
//
// Entry weight = the loan's cost in the first quarter we saw it, summed over
// all of its pieces. Every metric is weighted by entry cost.
//
// Right-censoring: at age k a cohort only counts loans whose vintage date is
// at least k quarters before their BDC's latest filing (n_loans_eligible,
// eligible_cost_b). Points with fewer than 20 eligible loans (30 for one BDC)
// or under 25% of the cohort's cost eligible are not published, so a curve
// simply stops. pct_eligible shows how much of the cohort is counted.
//
// Chained cumulative rates: each age adds only the NEW events at that age,
// measured on the loans old enough to reach it; earlier ages keep the rate
// measured on the larger group. So a cumulative rate never falls just because
// the old-enough group shrinks at a cohort's oldest ages. Survival is chained
// the same way and never rises.
//
// Unknown non-accrual flags: a loan whose latest status at age k is unknown
// (the BDC's NA marks were not captured that quarter) is left out of
// pct_ever_na / pct_ever_default and their HC / 1L variants at that age
// (never counted as performing). pct_na_unknown is that excluded share;
// pct_na_history_gap is the share counted as clear but with an earlier
// unknown quarter. na_partial = the two together are >= 5% of eligible cost.
//
//   pct_ever_na      = cumulative % of eligible cohort cost ever flagged
//                      non-accrual by age T (on-book only).
//   pct_ever_default = cumulative % ever non-accrual OR exited in distress
//                      (last mark < 0.85, or ever NA / below 80 before exit).
//                      Directionally comparable to Raymond James's
//                      "cumulative 1L default exposure" (ours spans all
//                      instruments; the _1l field is first lien only).
//   pct_ever_b80     = cumulative % ever marked < 80¢ on the dollar, among
//                      loans with a price mark by then (no par = left out).
//   pct_ever_modified= cumulative % with any modification event, among loans
//                      whose modification history could be judged
//                      (pct_mod_unknown = the share left out; mod_partial
//                      when it is >= 5%). Null when nothing could be judged.
//   pct_b90_alive    = % of the cost observed at age T that has a price mark
//                      (fair value ÷ par, scripts/marks.py) and is marked
//                      < 90¢; null when none has one. b90_mark_coverage_pct =
//                      that marked cost as % of all cost observed at age T.
//   pct_surviving    = % of eligible entry cost still on the book at age T
//                      (seen at age T or later). Never above 100%.
//
// is_partial: the vintage predates most of our filing coverage (survivors only).
//
// High-confidence (_hc) fields are published only when the HIGH+MED subset
// has 15+ eligible loans AND carries at least 25% of the counted cost
// (hc_cost_share). A figure resting on a sliver of the cohort is null.
// cohort_estimated_b = cost of loans dated by an ESTIMATE (name match, sibling
// facility, DERA floor, tenor model, first sighting). cohort_low_tier_b also
// includes disclosed dates that drifted, so it is not "estimated".

